# git-rebase-todo that reproduces this branch: ALLOC_UNMAPPED v4 backported
# from mm-new onto v7.2-rc5.  This is the minimal set - 25 prerequisite patches
# plus the cover letter and the 26 series patches.
#
# Rationale for every line, and all eight conflict resolutions, are in
# alloc-unmapped-backport-notes.md (section numbers referenced below) and in the
# "[ Backport to v7.2-rc5: ... ]" blocks of the individual commit messages.
#
# Usage (e.g. to redo this against a newer master):
#   git fetch origin master alloc-unmapped
#   git switch -c alloc-unmapped-master origin/alloc-unmapped
#   GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR="cp $PWD/alloc-unmapped-backport-rebase-todo" \
#       git rebase -i --keep-empty --onto origin/master origin/master
#
# --onto origin/master origin/master makes git enumerate origin/master..HEAD into
# the generated todo; the sequence editor then replaces it with these 52 lines.
# --keep-empty is needed for the empty b4 cover-letter commit.
# Order below is oldest-first (mm-new order), which is also a valid topological
# order - the prerequisite series conflict with each other if reordered.

